"view.prenatal.help"                    = "The PreNatal technique (developed by Eg Sneek) projects astronomical events during the gestation period onto the life of the individual.\n\nSelect the types of moment to include: mutual aspects between the selected planets, solar and lunar eclipses, sign ingresses, and stations (retrograde or direct).\n\nClick 'Change factors' to choose which planets are used for aspects, ingresses, and stations. Click 'Change aspects' to choose which aspect types are considered.\n\nPress 'Calculate' to compute the prenatal moments. The standard conception date is approximately 273 days before birth.\n\nIn the results table the 'Actual date' column shows when the prenatal moment becomes effective in the person's life, according to the conversion formula. The 'Prenatal date' shows when it occurred during gestation.";

